[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) merged every report about wrong dates as one issue and marked it known.
Read against its tenants and its own reports, it is three problems. Each one now has its own
ticket with its count.

<Callout kind="warn">
Fixing the parser closes one of the three. Ask which ticket a date report belongs to before you
merge it into #4471.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<SplitTable ticket={4471} />

## The three causes

**parser** ([#1](https://github.com/PedAltuve/mega-dev-kb/issues/1), fixed). The shared parser reads every date month first, and every tenant in #4471 writes the
day first. Day and month swap. It covers app and email reports everywhere, and booking-form
reports at tenants on `booking-v2`, whose hint already says `DD/MM/YYYY`.

**hint** ([#2](https://github.com/PedAltuve/mega-dev-kb/issues/2), won't fix: booking-v3 is retired). The `booking-v3` form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type month first,
as told, and the form reads the date the tenant's way. It only shows up in booking-form reports
from tenants on `booking-v3`. A parser fix does not touch it.

**one-day** ([#3](https://github.com/PedAltuve/mega-dev-kb/issues/3), open). A few bookings move by one day: Tuesday shows as Monday, an invite arrives before
the booking, one client gets Tuesday and another in Toronto gets Monday. A swap cannot do that;
time zones can. The desk already listed these reports (`oneDayMove` in `desk-notes.json`). Its view
counts them under their tenant's cause, so the table does too, and gives them a row of their own.

## How to tell them apart

- Go by the tenant and the way the report came in, never by intake's tag. Intake guesses from the
  reporter's browser, so an `en-US` browser at a day-first tenant gets `hint` either way.
- A date that moved by one day belongs to #3, whatever cause its tenant files it under.
- The export repeats reports across pages: count each id once.
- The subject line tells you nothing here. Every subject the hint and one-day reports use also
  appears in parser reports ("Month and day swapped?" among them), so
  [decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges all three into one ticket.

